# One shell command per line, run from the repo root. Lines starting with # are
# ignored.
#
# WHEN THIS LIST ACTUALLY RUNS, because the header used to say "non-zero exit
# refuses the push to develop/main" and that was never true in this repo:
# develop/main/master are refused OUTRIGHT by githooks/pre-push, before any check
# runs, precisely so that no check can earn the push. And a feature branch falls
# through the direct-push allowance, which this repo deliberately does not have.
#
# So the one thing that runs this list is a HAND RUN - `sh githooks/pre-push` -
# which is what AGENTS.md and complete-story tell a session to do before
# committing. That is the gate, and it is a real one.
#
# It was NOT real until 2026-08-14. race-timer was carrying a copy of the driver
# from before cairn added hand-run support on 2026-08-07, and a hand run against
# that copy fell straight through and exited 0 having printed nothing and run
# nothing - the documented gate reporting success without checking. Found by a
# review of #160 and fixed by porting the canonical driver back. Both halves of
# the lesson are in cairn `documented-is-not-installed`: the file was present,
# correct-looking, and every symptom was an absence.
#
# --no-watch-fs --rerun-tasks is not optional here. Gradle's file-watcher goes
# stale on this machine and reports BUILD SUCCESSFUL on a suite it never
# compiled - compileTestKotlin UP-TO-DATE on a file edited seconds earlier. That
# is the one hazard in cairn's Windows list that fails with a PASS rather than
# an error, so a gate without these flags can go green on code it never ran.
# See memory/global/windows-shell-hazards-2026-08-01.md.
./gradlew :shared:test --no-watch-fs --rerun-tasks
#
# #160 put the watch module's orchestration under test, and the step goes in BOTH
# places on purpose: a local gate that runs a different graph from CI is green on
# one machine and red on the other for reasons outside the tracked tree. Measured
# at ~10 s warm, which is the whole argument for it being here and
# :wear:assembleDebug not.
#
# :phone:testDebugUnitTest is NOT here, and that is a gap rather than a decision -
# it costs about the same and CI runs it. Left alone because #160 is not the issue
# in which to change what the phone module's gate is; noted so the absence reads
# as unfinished rather than considered.
./gradlew :wear:testDebugUnitTest --no-watch-fs --rerun-tasks
#
# :wear:assembleDebug is deliberately NOT here. CI runs it and it costs minutes;
# a pre-push slow enough to be worth skipping gets skipped, and a gate that is
# routinely bypassed protects nothing.
